{
 "result": "fibmod.py is a fast-doubling Fibonacci mod 1e9+7. It reads whitespace-separated integers from stdin, computes fib(n) per value by scanning the bits of n from the top (a, b = F(k), F(k+1); each bit doubles k and optionally adds one), and prints one result per line. It passes the public sample (in-0 matches out-0) and was accepted by assay at baseline 2.42867, noise 4.2%. Two variants (dropping a modulo, memoizing inputs, and a bit-shift loop) did not beat it beyond noise, so I am keeping the incumbent and resting to return unspent energy.",
